   $q$Listen. A windmill has big blades that look like the arms of a giant fan. When the wind blows, it pushes on the blades and makes them spin around and around. Long ago, the spinning blades turned heavy stones inside the mill, and the stones crushed grain into flour. Today, many tall windmills, often called wind turbines, make electricity instead. What makes the blades of a windmill spin? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"the moon","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"the moon"}},{"text":"the wind","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"the wind"}},{"text":"the rain","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"the rain"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$the wind$q$, $q$The wind pushes on the blades and makes them spin. The spinning blades once turned stones to make flour, and now many make electricity.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
