   $q$Listen. Dad fills a pot with water, puts it on the stove, and turns up the heat. Soon the water gets so hot that it bubbles and boils. Some of the water turns into steam, which rises up out of the pot. When the steam touches the lid, it turns back into tiny drops of water. The drops roll down and drip back into the pot. What makes the water turn into steam? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"ice","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"ice"}},{"text":"a spoon","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"a spoon"}},{"text":"heat","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"heat"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$heat$q$, $q$The heat from the stove makes the water boil, and some of it turns into steam. On the lid, the steam turns back into drops.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
