   $q$Listen. Earthworms live under the ground in the soil. As they wiggle along, they dig lots of little tunnels. The tunnels let air and rain water get down deep into the soil. Worms also eat old dead leaves, and the waste they leave behind makes the soil rich. Plant roots can grow strong and healthy in this soil. How do worm tunnels help the soil? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"let in air and water","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"let in air and water"}},{"text":"keep out the rain","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"keep out the rain"}},{"text":"make it freeze","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"make it freeze"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$let in air and water$q$, $q$Worms dig tunnels as they wiggle. The tunnels let air and rain water get deep into the soil, so roots can grow.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
