   $q$Listen. In spring, many apple trees are covered with white and pink flowers. Bees fly from flower to flower to sip a sweet juice called nectar. As they go, a yellow dust called pollen sticks to their fuzzy bodies and rubs off on other flowers. The pollen that bees carry helps the flowers make fruit. Later, many of those flowers grow into apples. What can the flowers grow into after bees visit? Tap the picture.$q$, $q$[{"text":"nut","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"nut","count":1}},{"text":"apple","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"apple","count":1}},{"text":"egg","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"egg","count":1}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$apple$q$, $q$Bees carry pollen from flower to flower. The pollen helps the flowers make fruit, and many of them grow into apples.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
