   $q$Listen. To make applesauce, first wash the apples and peel off the skins. Next, a grown up cuts the apples into chunks and takes out the seeds. Then the chunks cook in a pot with a little water until they are very soft. Soft apples are easy to mash, so last, you mash them with a big spoon until the sauce is smooth and thick. Why do the apples cook until they are soft? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"so they get hard","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"so they get hard"}},{"text":"so they turn blue","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"so they turn blue"}},{"text":"so they mash easily","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"so they mash easily"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$so they mash easily$q$, $q$Cooking makes the apple chunks very soft. Soft apples are easy to mash into smooth applesauce.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
