   $q$Listen. Long ago, people washed all their clothes by hand. They scrubbed each shirt on a bumpy board in a tub of soapy water, and it was very hard work. Then they twisted out the water and hung the clothes outside to dry. Later, washing machines were invented to do the scrubbing. The machines saved families many hours of hard work each week. How did washing machines help people? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"made clothes dirty","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"made clothes dirty"}},{"text":"saved time and work","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"saved time and work"}},{"text":"cooked their food","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"cooked their food"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$saved time and work$q$, $q$Washing by hand took a long time and was hard work. Washing machines did the scrubbing, so they saved people time and work.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
