   $q$Listen. Light from the sun travels in straight lines. When you stand outside on a sunny day, your body blocks some of that light. Light cannot get through you, so a dark shape forms on the ground. That dark shape is called your shadow. Late in the day, when the sun is low in the sky, shadows stretch out very long. What makes your shadow? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"you block the light","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"you block the light"}},{"text":"the rain falls","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"the rain falls"}},{"text":"the wind blows","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"the wind blows"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$you block the light$q$, $q$Your body blocks some of the sunlight. The light cannot get through you, so a dark shadow forms on the ground.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
