   $q$Listen. Many new roads are built in steps. First, big machines clear away trees and rocks. Next, workers press the dirt flat, so it is smooth and hard. Then they spread a thick layer of gravel, which is lots of small stones. Last, machines spread hot, black asphalt on top, and it cools into a smooth, hard road. What do workers spread right after they press the dirt flat? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"asphalt","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"asphalt"}},{"text":"grass seed","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"grass seed"}},{"text":"gravel","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"gravel"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$gravel$q$, $q$After the dirt is pressed flat, workers spread gravel, which is small stones. The hot asphalt goes on last, on top of the gravel.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
