   $q$Listen. Owl and Fox planned a picnic on the grassy hill. Owl packed an umbrella, just in case. Fox laughed and said, Look at the sunny sky, we will not need that! At lunch, dark clouds rolled in, and rain poured down. Fox got soaking wet, but Owl stayed nice and dry, and Fox said, Next time, I will be ready too. What is the lesson of this story? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Be brave","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Be brave"}},{"text":"Plan ahead","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Plan ahead"}},{"text":"Tell the truth","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Tell the truth"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Plan ahead$q$, $q$Owl brought an umbrella before the rain came, so Owl stayed dry. Fox did not get ready and got wet. The lesson is plan ahead.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
