   $q$Listen. Rabbit liked to tell everyone, Look at me, I am the best jumper in the whole forest! Rabbit said it to Frog, to Bird, and even to the trees. One day, Rabbit was so busy showing off a giant jump that Rabbit landed right in a muddy pond. Splash! The animals giggled, and Rabbit, dripping wet, decided to stop showing off. What is the lesson of this story? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Plan ahead","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Plan ahead"}},{"text":"Do not brag","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Do not brag"}},{"text":"Work as a team","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Work as a team"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Do not brag$q$, $q$Rabbit kept saying, I am the best, and showing off. Then Rabbit landed in the mud. The lesson is do not brag.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
