   $q$Listen. Hippo told Mouse, I will come to your party on Saturday. On Saturday, Hippo's friends asked Hippo to go swimming instead. Hippo wanted to swim, but Hippo remembered what Hippo had told Mouse. So Hippo walked all the way to the party and brought a big cake. Mouse was so happy to see Hippo there, just as Hippo had said. What is the lesson of this story? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Keep your word","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Keep your word"}},{"text":"Be patient","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Be patient"}},{"text":"Slow and steady wins","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Slow and steady wins"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keep your word$q$, $q$Hippo said, I will come to your party, and even when swimming sounded fun, Hippo went. The lesson is keep your word: do what you say you will do.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
