   $q$Listen. Kofi was carrying a big basket of yams up the hill all alone. The basket was so heavy that Kofi kept stopping to rest. Kofi's friends Ada and Sam walked by, but Kofi did not want to look weak, so Kofi said nothing. At last, Kofi called out, Can you lift one side? With a friend on each side, the basket went up the hill quickly. What is the lesson of this story? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ask for help","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Ask for help"}},{"text":"Be thankful","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Be thankful"}},{"text":"Do not brag","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Do not brag"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ask for help$q$, $q$Kofi struggled alone until Kofi asked the friends to lift. Then the basket went up fast. The lesson is ask for help when you need it.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
