   $q$Why does the author explain yeast in the second paragraph before explaining how the dough rises?$q$, $q$[{"text":"So readers know that yeast is easy to see","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"So readers know what makes the gas in the dough","is_correct":true},{"text":"To show that yeast is more important than flour","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To compare the yeast in two different kinds of bread","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$So readers know what makes the gas in the dough$q$, $q$The second paragraph explains that yeast gives off a gas as it eats, so the next paragraphs make sense when the gas forms bubbles and the dough puffs up. The passage says you need a microscope to see yeast, so it is not easy to see.$q$, 'draft', '7e197df4-7903-5d3e-9683-a4aff5e11bfa')
