   $q$Before reading, Kai thought the desert was a boring place with nothing to see. Which detail from the passage would the author use to show Kai a different view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"During the day, most animals hide under rocks to stay cool.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-wrong-view"},{"text":"The sun is hot, and the sand glows pale yellow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-wrong-view"},{"text":"An owl with yellow eyes sits on a cactus and watches the ground.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The desert looks empty once more when morning comes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-wrong-view"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An owl with yellow eyes sits on a cactus and watches the ground.$q$, $q$The owl watching from the cactus is one of the night sights that show the desert is full of things to see. The details about hiding animals and the empty morning would make the desert seem boring, which matches Kai's view instead of changing it.$q$, 'draft', '269f532d-ec03-503a-9a39-be42ef1e29ec')
