-- Passage rg3-connections-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1412d2d7-8387-520e-a482-2e18740707c6', 'rg3-connections-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-connections'), null,
        '3-5', $q$From Egg to Butterfly$q$, $q$A butterfly does not start its life with wings. Its life has four stages, and its body changes shape as it grows. Each stage leads to the next one.

First, a butterfly lays a tiny egg on a leaf. The leaf is not chosen by chance. It is the kind of leaf the baby will need to eat.

Next, the egg hatches, and a caterpillar crawls out. The caterpillar is very hungry. It eats the leaf it was born on, and then it eats more leaves. Because it eats so much, it grows quickly. Its skin gets too tight, so it sheds the old skin many times.

When the caterpillar is fully grown, it stops eating. Often, it hangs upside down from a twig. Then it forms a hard case around its body. This case is called a chrysalis. From the outside, the chrysalis looks still. Inside, the caterpillar's body is changing into a new shape.

After about two weeks, the chrysalis splits open. A butterfly climbs out. At first its wings are wet and folded. The butterfly pumps fluid into its wings so they open wide. Once the wings are dry, the butterfly can fly.

Finally, the grown butterfly finds a mate and lays eggs of its own. Then the whole cycle begins again.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
