   $q$The passage says that seeds "can still take a trip." What does this mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Seeds can only stay in one spot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Seeds can fall and get hurt.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"},{"text":"Seeds can pack bags for a vacation.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Seeds can move to new places.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Seeds can move to new places.$q$, $q$The next sentence says plants "send their seeds to new places," so taking a trip means moving somewhere new. Seeds do not really go on vacations.$q$, 'draft', '1d3ea69f-6b74-54ac-840e-308e7bc6e9da')
