-- Passage rg3-figurative-language-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('dac957a5-dff8-5d38-a8c1-2ba349dfc8be', 'rg3-figurative-language-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-figurative-language'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Frozen Frog$q$, $q$Zara and Mateo were building a game on the class tablet. In the game, a little frog hopped across lily pads to reach the other side of a pond.

"Let's test it," Mateo said. Zara tapped the start button. The frog jumped once and then froze. It would not move at all.

"Our game is broken," Zara groaned. "We have been working on this forever."

Mateo leaned closer to the screen. "Let's put on our thinking caps," Mateo said. "There has to be a reason."

The two friends read their code one line at a time. They read it slowly, like detectives looking for clues. Then Zara spotted the problem. One block told the frog to jump only one time, instead of every time the player tapped.

Zara changed the block, and Mateo tapped start again. This time, the frog bounced from pad to pad all the way across the pond.

"It works!" Mateo shouted. Zara let out a sigh of relief. The bug that had been driving them up the wall was finally gone.

Their teacher, Mr. Haddad, walked by and watched the frog hop. "Nice work," Mr. Haddad said. "Fixing mistakes is a big part of coding. You two stuck with it, and it paid off."$q$, 'draft')
