   $q$"'Our game is broken,' Zara groaned." Why does the author use "groaned" instead of "said"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to show that Zara felt cheerful and proud","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-shade-of-meaning"},{"text":"to show that Zara was asking a question","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-text"},{"text":"to show that Zara felt upset and frustrated","is_correct":true},{"text":"to show that Zara whispered a secret","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-shade-of-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to show that Zara felt upset and frustrated$q$, $q$To groan is to make a low, unhappy sound, and the frog has just stopped working, so Zara is frustrated. A whisper is quiet, but it does not show an unhappy feeling the way a groan does.$q$, 'draft', 'dac957a5-dff8-5d38-a8c1-2ba349dfc8be')
